  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\frac{x}{2}}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}{e}^{y}, & \\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡9, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le 1,0\\le Y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡9).$",
